        "t": "chr",
        "v": [
          "This module checks whether each extracted data column is documented in a codebook or README, and flags documented variables that never appear in the data.",
          "We examined 1 codebook/README/label source and 20 data columns across 1 file.",
          "#### Column Documentation",
          "::: {.panel-tabset}\n\n## survey.csv\n\n\n```{r}\n#| echo: false\n\n\n# table data --------------------------------------\ntable <- structure(list(Column = c(\"TIPI_2\", \"TIPI_3\", \"TIPI_4\", \"TIPI_5\", \n\"Duration (in seconds)\", \"EndDate\", \"Finished\", \"Progress\", \"Q1_DO_order\", \n\"Q2_TEXT\", \"Q8timing_Click.Count\", \"Q8timing_First.Click\", \"Q8timing_Last.Click\", \n\"Q8timing_Page.Submit\", \"RecordedDate\", \"ResponseId\", \"StartDate\", \n\"Status\", \"TIPI_1\", \"age\"), Documented = c(\"no\", \"no\", \"no\", \n\"no\", \"yes\", \"yes\", \"yes\", \"yes\", \"yes\", \"yes\", \"yes\", \"yes\", \n\"yes\", \"yes\", \"yes\", \"yes\", \"yes\", \"yes\", \"yes\", \"yes\"), Label = c(NA, \nNA, NA, NA, \"Export machinery / paradata column (not a measured variable).\", \n\"Export machinery / paradata column (not a measured variable).\", \n\"Export machinery / paradata column (not a measured variable).\", \n\"Export machinery / paradata column (not a measured variable).\", \n\"Export machinery / paradata column (not a measured variable).\", \n\"Other please specify\", \"Export machinery / paradata column (not a measured variable).\", \n\"Export machinery / paradata column (not a measured variable).\", \n\"Export machinery / paradata column (not a measured variable).\", \n\"Export machinery / paradata column (not a measured variable).\", \n\"Export machinery / paradata column (not a measured variable).\", \n\"Export machinery / paradata column (not a measured variable).\", \n\"Export machinery / paradata column (not a measured variable).\", \n\"Export machinery / paradata column (not a measured variable).\", \n\"Extraverted enthusiastic\", \"Age in years\"), \"Codebook Variable\" = c(NA, \nNA, NA, NA, \"Duration (in seconds)\", \"EndDate\", \"Finished\", \"Progress\", \n\"Q1_DO_order\", \"Q2_TEXT\", \"Q8timing_Click.Count\", \"Q8timing_First.Click\", \n\"Q8timing_Last.Click\", \"Q8timing_Page.Submit\", \"RecordedDate\", \n\"ResponseId\", \"StartDate\", \"Status\", \"TIPI_1\", \"age\"), Source = c(NA, \nNA, NA, NA, NA, NA, NA, NA, NA, \"codebook.csv\", NA, NA, NA, NA, \nNA, NA, NA, NA, \"codebook.csv\", \"codebook.csv\"), Status = c(\"unlabelled\", \n\"unlabelled\", \"unlabelled\", \"unlabelled\", \"labelled\", \"labelled\", \n\"labelled\", \"labelled\", \"labelled\", \"labelled\", \"labelled\", \"labelled\", \n\"labelled\", \"labelled\", \"labelled\", \"labelled\", \"labelled\", \"labelled\", \n\"labelled\", \"labelled\")), row.names = c(NA, 20L), class = \"data.frame\")\n\n# display table -----------------------------------\nmetacheck::report_table(table, \"auto\", 25, FALSE)\n```\n\n\n:::",
          "#### Scales",
          "We detected 1 column group (by shared abbreviation) that look like scales; 1 was matched to a named instrument from the paper text or dictionary. Groups we could not name are listed too — they are real scale-like column families whose instrument the manuscript did not identify. Identified scales are exported in the OpenScales OSD structure.",
          "\n```{r}\n#| echo: false\n\n\n# table data --------------------------------------\ntable <- structure(list(File = \"survey.csv\", Abbrev = \"TIPI\", Columns = 5L, \n    \"Max item\" = \"5\", Scale = \"Ten Item Personality Inventory\", \n    Confidence = \"medium\", Source = \"matched\"), row.names = c(NA, \n-1L), class = \"data.frame\")\n\n# display table -----------------------------------\nmetacheck::report_table(table, \"auto\", 40, FALSE)\n```\n",
          "To let this tool (and anyone reusing the data) identify these scales with **high confidence**:\n- **Name the instrument in the manuscript with its abbreviation** — e.g. \"the Breakup Distress Scale (BDS)\" — matching the column prefix.\n- **Add a codebook** giving the item wording, or state the number of items (\"a 15-item scale\")."
        ]
